config SERVICE_SHARED_PRF_STORAGE
    bool "Shared PRF storage"
    help
      Shared storage used by the PRF (recovery) firmware.

if SERVICE_SHARED_PRF_STORAGE

config SERVICE_SHARED_PRF_STORAGE_IMPORT_STOCK_V2
    bool "Import the stock firmware's v2 shared PRF storage"
    depends on BT
    help
      On boards whose recovery firmware is the stock one, which keeps its own
      shared PRF storage in the older v2 layout (snowy): one struct at the
      start of PART_STOCK_SHARED_PRF_STORAGE, with Bluetopia's legacy pairing
      keys. Copy its root keys, name and pairing into this firmware's storage
      when the identity root key differs from it, so the phone sees one watch
      in both firmwares. The stock region is only read.

module = SERVICE_SHARED_PRF_STORAGE
module-str = Shared PRF storage
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_level"

endif
